course: dictionary
lesson: 2074
title: Constipation: a word about your body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Health lessons use some words about the body. Constipation is a noun, so it names a problem that a body can have. Its clues are in the sentences: «Fruit, vegetables, whole grains and water help with constipation, which is common.» Help tells you it is a problem that can be fixed, and common tells you that lots of people get it.
explain: «Constipation means hard poo that is difficult to pass; water, fruit, vegetables and wholegrains help, and holding it in makes it worse.» Read the clue words: hard, difficult, help, worse. They all point to the same idea: the poo is stuck, and food and drink that are good for you can free it.
explain: Some body troubles are not something to be embarrassed about. «Some body troubles are common and nothing to be ashamed of, like constipation or wetting the bed, but some signs, like blood in wee or poo, always need a doctor.» The word but tells you the sentence is changing direction, so the second half is the important warning.
fact: Constipation means you cannot poo easily or often, because your poo is hard and dry.
fact: You can say you suffer from constipation, or that you are constipated.
fact: Drinking water, eating fruit, vegetables and fibre, and being active help to prevent constipation.
fact: Constipation is common and nothing to be ashamed of, like wetting the bed.
fact: Blood in wee or poo always needs a doctor, so tell a grown-up straight away.
exercise: «Constipation means hard poo that is difficult to pass.» What does constipation mean? | *Trouble pooing easily or often, because the poo is hard and dry | A tummy ache from a cold | Feeling sick after eating a big lunch
exercise: Which of these helps to prevent constipation? | Holding it in until later | Lying in bed all day | *Drinking water and eating fruit and vegetables | Eating only sweets
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Fruit, vegetables, whole grains and water help with constipation, which is common.» that tells you many people get it. | whole | *common | fruit | water
test: Which phrase means you have trouble pooing? | *Be constipated | Be thirsty | Be ashamed | Be well
test: Which of these must you always tell a doctor about? | Constipation that is common | *Blood in wee or poo | Wetting the bed sometimes | Feeling hungry after sport
exam: Ella reads «Some body troubles are common and nothing to be ashamed of.» What does ashamed mean? | Very tired and sleepy | Proud and happy | Cold and wet | *Embarrassed or bad about something
